# Example site settings for setup-server.sh.  Copy to `site.env` (which is
# git-ignored) and edit.  This file is the template; the real one names a host.

# Public name Caddy serves.  An A/AAAA record must already point at the box.
# No DNS at hand?  sslip.io encodes the IPv4 address, e.g. 203-0-113-7.sslip.io
DOMAIN=example.org

# Database files inside /srv/sylphd/db (installed by hand, not by this repo).
# Every file listed here must exist before setup-server.sh runs; it stops with
# an error naming a missing one.  One database:
# SYLPH_DB=gtdb-r232-c200-dbv2.syl2db
# SYLPH_META=meta-r232-reps.sqlite
#
# Several databases: a space-separated list.  Each entry is FILE, or NAME=FILE
# to give it a short display name (`/info` and the web page show the names).
# The server profiles against all of them as one pool.  Quote the value; file
# names cannot contain whitespace, and NAME uses letters, digits, '_', '.' and
# '-'.
# SYLPH_DB="gtdb=gtdb-r232-c200-dbv2.syl2db uhgv=uhgv_c200_dbv1.syldb fungi=fungi-refseq-2025-10-11-c200-dbv1.syldb"
# SYLPH_META=meta-r232-reps.sqlite

# Site policy for `sylphd serve` — see deploy/sylphd.service for what the
# flags mean.  One whitespace-separated string, no quoting inside it.
# Quote the value (this file is sourced by bash).  A public instance should
# also cap contigs per request: one /contigs request is one job and its
# contigs run one after the other, and on a server with plain databases a
# contig costs ~0.6 s, so the 4096 default could occupy a job slot for ~40
# minutes.  --max-contigs 100 keeps one client's request around a minute, and
# the CLI and the web page batch by the advertised limits.max_contigs.
# SYLPH_SERVE_ARGS="--allow-sequences --max-jobs 2 --max-contigs 100 --max-queue 16 --rate-limit 10/min --trusted-proxy unix --cors-origin *"

# Optional: keep opt-in usage statistics (counts per 10-minute window, never
# addresses or names; public at /usage).  Off unless the flag is added to
# SYLPH_SERVE_ARGS above; the directory is created by setup-server.sh and
# writable for the service:
# SYLPH_SERVE_ARGS="... --usage-db /srv/sylphd/usage/usage.sqlite"

# Optional: describe the instance on the web page.  The display name may
# contain spaces; the about file is Markdown, editable without a restart.
# SYLPH_NAME="GTDB r232"
# SYLPH_SERVE_ARGS="... --about /etc/sylphd/about.md"

# Largest request body Caddy accepts (Caddyfile request_body max_size).
# SYLPH_HTTP_MAX=64MB
